                <pb facs="0284" n="194" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav02/pg194"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 861.00/1980</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-06-07T19:00:00+02:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1918, 7
                                p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received June 8, 11.55 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1708. Department’s 1395. De Giers, Russian Ambassador,
                    states that he is now able to communicate with Russian political men in <pb
                        facs="0285" n="195" xml:id="pg195"/> Russia and get a reply within a week.
                    He says that he received information yesterday that all parties from socialists
                    to Cadets and moderate monarchists are together. They cannot ask that military
                    expedition be sent, but hope it will. He gave me a report from General Miller, ex-commandant of army corps of
                    southern Russia, and Colonel Niemchenko, who was attached
                    to the Russian administration for military supplies in Italy, upon a possible
                    Allied military entry and establishment in Russia. Report sent by mail.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d253-f1"/></p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson
                            Page</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
